of encephalitic conditions mediated by var-
ious autoimmune disorders. Anti-glutamic
acid decarboxylase (GAD) antibody-associ-
ated AE is an extremely rare condition which is char-
acterized by the acute or subacute onset of seizures,
memory deficits, cognitive impairment and psychiatric
symptoms." Meanwhile, the association between an-
ti-GAD and Stiff-Person Syndrome (SPS) is well known.
SPS is characterized by progressive rigidity and muscle
spasms affecting the axial and limb muscles, predomi-
nantly in females.'?! Here, we report a rare case of anti-
